---
import PhotoPlaceholder from '../PhotoPlaceholder.astro';
import SectionHead from '../SectionHead.astro';
---

<section class="band-cream section">
  <SectionHead num="7 / 14 — Place" heading="Beyond the living room." />

  <div class="container-page">
    <PhotoPlaceholder
      description="A neighborhood plaza in the Valley — a Sunday market, kids and adults using public space together. Not the Strip. A version of Henderson Town Square or downtown's Symphony Park, on a regular weekend."
    />
  </div>

  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="vision-prose">
      <p>
        We want tree-lined bike paths. We want bus stops with shade. We want buildings on streets
        that invite you to stay, not just rush through. We want parks within walking distance of
        every neighborhood — not just one big regional park forty minutes away. We want plazas wide
        enough for a Sunday market, libraries open evenings and weekends, community centers that
        look like front porches instead of DMV offices. We want festivals that close streets, not
        parking lots. We want sidewalks you can actually use in July.
      </p>
      <p>
        The won Valley has all of this distributed across its town centers, not centralized in one
        place. Public space becomes the third place — neither home nor work — where Las&nbsp;Vegans
        actually run into each other. That is what city life is supposed to feel like. It's also
        what the social-science research keeps finding: the loneliness epidemic gets less worse in
        places where people have somewhere to be that isn't their living room or their office. Vegas
        can have it. The desert is not the obstacle; the obstacle is that we never built for it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
